# Operational excellence (scorecard, SLOs, alerting)

Phased work and action IDs live in [docs/plans/operational-excellence.md](docs/plans/operational-excellence.md) (`OPS-*`). Treat that document as the backlog — **do not implement** PagerDuty escalate-if-unacked (`OPS-P3-002`) unless the user explicitly asks. Phase 0–4 (except `OPS-P3-002`) are done (`ALERT-*` Action Groups + living scorecard + monthly workflow + materials synthetics + field/lab FCP + Studio SLO cadence + CD Sev1 + inquiry SLI + IR stub + prod/shared KV purge protection + subscription budget at **125% of retail expected** + ACS monthly digest).

## Azure cost estimate + subscription budget (required on infra change)

Whenever you **add, remove, or change billable Azure resources** (Terraform in `infra/**`: SKUs/tiers, counts, regions, web-test frequency/locations, ACS phone numbers, App Insights caps, storage, etc.), in the **same change**:

1. **Recalculate expected monthly cost** from **Azure retail** Consumption rates for the **region(s) actually deployed** (default **eastus2**). Prefer `https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices` (or Azure MCP `pricing`) over stale docs. Sum steady-state usage (fixed SKUs + metered drivers such as web-test executions); exclude one-off incident SMS/voice unless you are provisioning a always-on number/lease.
2. **Update** [`docs/runbooks/cost-and-quotas.md`](docs/runbooks/cost-and-quotas.md) with the full **USD breakdown table**, **expected total**, **last-calculated date**, and unit rates used. Keep non-Azure lines (Gemini, GitHub) separate from the Azure total.
3. **Set the subscription budget** to **125% of expected**, rounded **up** to a whole USD dollar:  
   `subscription_budget_usd = ceil(expected_monthly_usd * 1.25)` in [`infra/bootstrap/budget.tf`](infra/bootstrap/budget.tf) (`budget-elyse-portfolio-monthly`).
4. **Keep Actual cost alert thresholds at 80% and 100%** of that budget amount (emails → Key Vault `ALERT-EMAIL` only). Do not drop the 80% notification. (80% of a 125% budget ≈ expected retail spend.)
5. **Sync** `SUBSCRIPTION_BUDGET_USD` in [`scripts/ops-scorecard-refresh.mjs`](scripts/ops-scorecard-refresh.mjs), plus budget mentions in `AGENTS.md`, [`docs/plans/operational-excellence.md`](docs/plans/operational-excellence.md), and `infra/bootstrap/README.md`.

Do **not** invent rates or leave `cost-and-quotas.md` as vague “negligible” when a meter has a material fixed cost (e.g. SWA Standard, standard web tests).

## Scorecard

- Rubric lives in the plan. Living scores: `docs/ops/operational-excellence-scorecard.md` (from `docs/ops/scorecard-evaluation.json` via `scripts/ops-scorecard-refresh.mjs`).
- Monthly refresh (`OPS-P0-004` / `OPS-P4-002`): `.github/workflows/ops-scorecard-monthly.yml` uses `scripts/mint-github-app-token.sh` (line-masked PEM), verifies Contents:write via mint response + `/installation/repositories`, pushes with App git credentials (`persist-credentials: false`), probes Cost Management spend/MoM vs the **current** subscription budget (see `cost-and-quotas.md` / `budget.tf`), and emails an ACS digest to `ALERT-EMAIL` + `SITE-CONTACT-EMAIL` (recipients never written into git artifacts). CD ignores scorecard-only pushes. Never reintroduce `GITHUB_TOKEN` pushes, PEM `with:` inputs, or multiline `::add-mask::$PEM`.
- Scorecard content is scores, evidence, gaps, and USD figures only — **never** alert emails, phones, or secrets.
- Subscription budget (`OPS-P4-001`): bootstrap `budget-elyse-portfolio-monthly` = **ceil(expected × 1.25)**; Actual **80%** / **100%** → `ALERT-EMAIL` only. Expected breakdown SoT: `docs/runbooks/cost-and-quotas.md`.

## Private details never in git

When planning or implementing alerts, on-call, or support contacts:

- **Never** commit real alert emails, SMS/voice numbers, PagerDuty/Better Stack routing keys, or similar private operator details in Terraform variables files, docs, examples, canvases, PR bodies, or source comments.
- Store them in **Azure Key Vault** and read at deploy/apply time (data sources / sync scripts), same pattern as `SITE-CONTACT-*` and ACS secrets (`lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }`, set via `az keyvault secret set`).
- Use placeholders only in the repo: `REPLACE_ME`, `<email>`, `+1XXXXXXXXXX`.
- Prefer dedicated **`ALERT-*`** secrets in **`kv-elyse-shared`** (bootstrap placeholders), not reuse of `SITE-CONTACT-EMAIL` / `SITE-CONTACT-PHONE` (those are inquiry notify via ACS). Monthly digests may email **both** `ALERT-EMAIL` and `SITE-CONTACT-EMAIL` via ACS **email** — do **not** put `SITE-CONTACT-EMAIL` on Azure Budget threshold notifications.
- Do **not** send ops/Sev1 alerts through ACS contact-form SMS.
- Action Groups read `ALERT-EMAIL` / `ALERT-SMS-PHONE` / `ALERT-VOICE-PHONE` at apply — do **not** reintroduce plaintext `alert_email` (or phone) Terraform variables.

## Keep the plan in sync

When you change scorecard dimensions/rubric, SLO targets, severity→channel mapping, alert secret names, budget amount / cost-estimate formula, or the monthly workflow contract, update `docs/plans/operational-excellence.md` in the same PR. Extend [rotate-secrets.md](docs/runbooks/rotate-secrets.md) when secret names change. After the living scorecard exists, update it (or let the monthly workflow commit do so) rather than only editing canvases.
